DERIVATIVE WORK NOTICE

This skill is a derivative work based on:

    Opposing Counsel Review
    Author: Larissa Meredith-Flister
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    Version: 2026-04-26

Larissa Meredith-Flister's skill supplies the adversarial method that this work depends
on: the instruction to attack rather than critique, the six-part analytical structure
(core theory of attack; reconstructed argument stripped of rhetoric; primary lines of
attack by category; the sceptical judge; surgical strikes; what the argument is trying to
hide), the formal British English register, and the prohibitions on hedging, balancing,
and inventing authority.

The additions in this work are: the second adversarial pass turned on the first pass's own
output; the ten named failure modes and their diagnostics; the one-sentence-reply and
credibility sustainability tests; the five-head ceiling; the rules on early concession and
on closing with what is not contested; and the output discipline that suppresses the
discarded first draft in favour of a standalone rebuilt attack.

No endorsement by Larissa Meredith-Flister of this derivative work is claimed or implied.

